FM-1 Chimera Vocal is made of parts under different licences. Each file says its own at its top (an SPDX line); the
full texts are in LICENSES/.

  Files                                                    Licence                         Copyright
  -------------------------------------------------------  ------------------------------  ------------------------------
  engine/, app/dsp/voice_male.h (the port of CHIMERA's     MIT (LICENSES/MIT-CHIMERA.txt)  Jameson Hodge (CHIMERA);
  voice)                                                                                   the C port: Shan-Sherif
  app/app.c, app/app.h, app/.github/ (started from         MPL-2.0 (LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt)  Charles Vestal (fm1-base's
  fm1-base's template)                                                                     template); Shan-Sherif
  app/web/, app/site/, app/docs/, app/tests/, tools/, lab/ MIT (LICENSES/MIT.txt)          Shan-Sherif
  engine/ch_dict_data.h, app/dsp/words_default.h           CMUdict's BSD-style licence     Carnegie Mellon University
  (CMU Pronouncing Dictionary entries)                     (LICENSES/CMUdict.txt)          (the entries)

Not in this repository, with their own licences: fm1-base and felucca-bsp (base/, a git submodule: MPL-2.0, including
code from Felucca by Leo Kuroshita and from Melodee by Kerem Kilic, both relicensed MPL-2.0 by their authors, and fonts
under the SIL OFL 1.1: see base/LICENSING.md); CHIMERA itself (external/, cloned for the lab: MIT); the JieLi AC79 SDK
files every FM-1 package carries (Apache-2.0, read from your SDK at build time).

The firmware package (chimera-X.Y.Z.fwsc) combines them: MPL-2.0 AND MIT, with the CMUdict entries under CMU's licence
and the SDK's files under Apache-2.0. The site ships those licence texts beside the package.

"CHIMERA" and the flat-view head are used with Jameson Hodge's permission
(https://github.com/jamesondh/chimera-vocal-synth/issues/104#issuecomment-6882133297). FM-1 Chimera Vocal is
unofficial: not affiliated with or endorsed by Jameson Hodge, M-VAVE, JieLi or fm1-base's authors. M-VAVE and FM-1 are
trademarks of their owners.
